<article class="env-definition" id="00PZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00PZ">Definition <span data-tag="00PZ">10.123.7</span>.</a> Given an inclusion of rings $R \subset S$ and an element $x \in S$ we say that $x$ is <em>strongly transcendental over $R$</em> if whenever $u(a_0 + a_1 x + \ldots + a_ k x^ k) = 0$ with $u \in S$ and $a_ i \in R$, then we have $ua_ i = 0$ for all $i$. </p>
